title = "O'Shaughnessy Dam"
text = "3,800 feet. Congress passed the Raker Act in 1913 to dam the Tuolumne River here for San Francisco's water supply, over John Muir's fierce opposition. The valley floor beneath the water once held oak groves and meadows much like Yosemite Valley."

